{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01TSe1J8z51VPQuFSjydTjCm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. The builder's global-constraints.txt only has `sentence-transformers<5.2.1` (not `transformers`). The torch-2.11.0 cpu-ubi9 constraints don't have any transformers constraint either.\n\nSo the only `transformers<5` constraint is in `collections/rhaiis/cpu-ubi9/constraints.txt` with the comment saying it was for AIPCC-9443.\n\nNow let me check what vllm 0.24.0 actually requires in terms of transformers, and also try to find the git history to confirm when vllm was updated.\nThe constraint comment claims vllm requires transformers<5, but that was apparently true for an older vllm version like 0.21.0. The current vllm 0.24.0 actually requires transformers>=5.6.0, which is the opposite constraint. I need to dig into the git history to see when vllm was upgraded and understand how this constraint became outdated.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":355,"cache_read_input_tokens":80540,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":355,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea133810-9e1f-4653-a656-18c578a01f91","uuid":"e4c8d285-66c9-4352-9ba3-a0d7a2c0904e","timestamp":"2026-07-20T22:01:18.011Z","request_id":"req_vrtx_011CdE4ab57DjfgwDmukSo9w"}
