{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01VegWptpwC1Wq9drAL7XoBi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"File writes are being blocked by the permission system across all paths. Per the harness instructions, I'll report this and present the full content of each deliverable as text output, demonstrating the analysis. The eval harness is blocking the Write tool calls — no workarounds will be attempted.\n\n---\n\n## RCA Analysis Complete — File Content Output\n\nNote: All Write tool calls were blocked by the permission system. The following is the content I would write to each file.\n\n---\n\n### `groups/02-fromager-bootstrap-fails-to-resolve-transformers-5-6-0/sections/error-overview.md`\n\n```markdown\nThe `rhaiis cpu-ubi9` bootstrap fails at approximately 90% completion when fromager cannot resolve a `transformers` dependency: the requirement `transformers>=5.6.0` (introduced by `vllm 0.24.0`) is irreconcilable with the collection's `transformers<5` constraint. Both the aarch64 and x86_64 variants fail with the identical error:\n\n​```error\n05:25:17 ERROR Unable to resolve requirement specifier transformers>=5.6.0 with constraint transformers<5 using PyPI resolver (searching at https://pypi.org/simple): found no match for transformers>=5.6.0 using PyPI resolver (searching at https://pypi.org/simple), searching for sdists, ignoring pre-release versions because found no match for transformers>=5.6.0 using PyPI resolver (searching at https://pypi.org/simple), searching for sdists, ignoring pre-release versions\n​```\n```\n\n---\n\n### `groups/02-fromager-bootstrap-fails-to-resolve-transformers-5-6-0/sections/root-cause.md`\n\n```markdown\nThe failure is caused by a stale version constraint in `collections/rhaiis/cpu-ubi9/constraints.txt`. The constraint `transformers<5` was originally added for AIPCC-9443 to prevent packages like `compressed-tensors` from pulling in `transformers` 5.x at a time when vllm required `transformers<5`. When vllm was subsequently bumped from 0.21.0 to 0.24.0+rhaiv.1 (AIPCC-17429, committed 2026-07-10), vllm's own transitive dependency changed to require `transformers>=5.6.0` — directly opposing the constraint that was originally added on its behalf. The constraint was not updated alongside the vllm version bump.\n\n**Failure Chain**\n\n1. `collections/rhaiis/cpu-ubi9/requirements.txt` pins `vllm==0.24.0+rhaiv.1`, which transitively requires `transformers>=5.6.0`.\n2. `collections/rhaiis/cpu-ubi9/constraints.txt` contains `transformers<5` (added for AIPCC-9443 based on requirements of the then-current vllm 0.21.x).\n3. Fromager's resolver cannot satisfy `transformers>=5.6.0 AND transformers<5` simultaneously — no candidate exists.\n4. Both `rhaiis-cpu-ubi9-x86_64` and `rhaiis-cpu-ubi9-aarch64` bootstrap jobs fail identically at this resolution step.\n\nThe constraint's own comment (`# AIPCC-9443: vllm requires transformers<5`) is now factually inverted — vllm 0.24.0 requires `transformers>=5.6.0`. Builder-level constraints (torch-2.11.0 cpu-ubi9 and global-constraints.txt) do not contain any `transformers<5` entry; the only source of the blocking constraint is the pipeline-repository collection file.\n```\n\n---\n\n### `groups/02-fromager-bootstrap-fails-to-resolve-transformers-5-6-0/sections/resolution.md`\n\n```markdown\nRemove the stale `transformers<5` constraint from the `rhaiis cpu-ubi9` constraint file. The constraint was added for the benefit of vllm 0.21.x but vllm 0.24.0 now requires `transformers>=5.6.0`, making the constraint self-defeating.\n\n**File: `collections/rhaiis/cpu-ubi9/constraints.txt`**\n```diff\n-# AIPCC-9443: vllm requires transformers<5; constrain to prevent compressed-tensors pulling in transformers 5.x\n-transformers<5\n```\n\nRemoving the line allows fromager to resolve `transformers` to the latest compatible version (5.6.x or newer), satisfying vllm 0.24.0's requirement.\n\n**Caveats**\n\nThe original constraint was also intended to prevent `compressed-tensors` from pulling in transformers 5.x. Before removing it, verify that no other package in the `rhaiis cpu-ubi9` collection explicitly requires `transformers<5`. If `compressed-tensors` has a hard upper-bound on transformers, the correct fix is to pin `transformers` to a specific 5.x version that satisfies both the lower bound from vllm and any upper bound from compressed-tensors. Builder-level global constraints do not set a `transformers` bound, so this change only affects `rhaiis cpu-ubi9`.\n```\n\n---\n\n### `groups/02-fromager-bootstrap-fails-to-resolve-transformers-5-6-0/sections/feedback.md`\n\n```markdown\n**Stale constraint invalidated by the package update it was meant to support**\n\nThe `transformers<5` constraint was explicitly annotated with the ticket and package it was added for (`AIPCC-9443: vllm requires transformers<5`). When vllm was bumped to 0.24.0 (AIPCC-17429), this constraint was not revisited. There is no automated check that, when a pinned package is updated, looks for constraints that were added because of that package's prior version requirements.\n\n**Expected**: when a constraint is tagged with the dependency that motivated it, updating that dependency should trigger a review of the associated constraint.\n\n**Encountered**: the constraint remained in place unchanged despite the vllm version update inverting the underlying rationale.\n\n**Gap**: a process or CI check that detects \"this constraint comment names a dependency that was just updated\" would have flagged this before the pipeline ran. Alternatively, keeping constraint comments tied to Jira tickets with a \"verify on vllm update\" reminder would surface the issue at update time.\n```\n\n---\n\n### `groups/02-fromager-bootstrap-fails-to-resolve-transformers-5-6-0/finding.json`\n\n```json\n{\n  \"group_id\": \"02-fromager-bootstrap-fails-to-resolve-transformers-5-6-0\",\n  \"title\": \"Stale transformers<5 constraint blocks vllm 0.24.0 bootstrap requiring transformers>=5.6.0\",\n  \"collections\": [\"rhaiis\"],\n  \"actions\": [\"bootstrap-and-onboard\"],\n  \"error_summary\": \"Fromager bootstrap fails: transformers>=5.6.0 (from vllm 0.24.0) is irreconcilable with constraint transformers<5 in rhaiis cpu-ubi9 constraints\",\n  \"suggested_resolution_summary\": \"Remove or update the transformers<5 constraint in collections/rhaiis/cpu-ubi9/constraints.txt to allow transformers>=5.6.0\",\n  \"has_resolution_file\": true,\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"confidence_justification\": \"The error message directly names both sides of the conflict (transformers>=5.6.0 and constraint transformers<5). The constraints file at the pipeline SHA was confirmed via GitLab API and contains the exact constraint with its AIPCC-9443 comment. The requirements file confirms vllm==0.24.0+rhaiv.1. Git history shows vllm was updated from 0.21.0 to 0.24.0 on 2026-07-10 (AIPCC-17429) without a corresponding constraint update. Both aarch64 and x86_64 jobs fail identically at the same resolution step. Builder-level constraints contain no transformers<5 entry, confirming the pipeline collection file is the sole source.\",\n  \"cascade\": false,\n  \"target_repo\": \"https://gitlab.com/redhat/rhel-ai/rhai/pipeline\",\n  \"target_repo_reason\": \"The fix requires removing the stale transformers<5 constraint from collections/rhaiis/cpu-ubi9/constraints.txt, which lives in the pipeline repository.\",\n  \"group_consistency\": \"consistent\",\n  \"feedback_status\": \"included\",\n  \"references\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"collections/rhaiis/cpu-ubi9/constraints.txt\",\n      \"description\": \"Contains the transformers<5 constraint with AIPCC-9443 comment — confirmed as the sole source of the blocking constraint\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"collections/rhaiis/cpu-ubi9/requirements.txt\",\n      \"description\": \"Confirms vllm==0.24.0+rhaiv.1 as the pinned vllm version — the version that introduced the incompatible transformers>=5.6.0 requirement\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"collections/rhaiis/cpu-ubi9/constraints-rules.txt\",\n      \"description\": \"Maps rhaiis cpu-ubi9 to torch-2.11.0 builder constraints — checked to identify all constraint sources for this collection\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"wheels/builder/collections/torch-2.11.0/cpu-ubi9/constraints.txt\",\n      \"description\": \"Checked for transformers constraints at the torch collection level — none found, confirming the constraint is only in the pipeline repo\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"wheels/builder/collections/global-constraints.txt\",\n      \"description\": \"Checked for global transformers constraints — only sentence-transformers<5.2.1 found, not transformers, confirming the blocking constraint is solely in the collection-level file\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"wheels/builder/overrides/settings/vllm.yaml\",\n      \"description\": \"Reviewed vllm build settings for dependency overrides — no transformers-related overrides found\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"resources_used\": {\n    \"agent_docs\": [],\n    \"skills\": [],\n    \"tools\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"glab API (repository/commits)\",\n        \"description\": \"Used to trace the git history for requirements.txt (found AIPCC-17429 updated vllm to 0.24.0 on 2026-07-10) and constraints.txt (confirmed constraint predates the vllm update), establishing the causal timeline\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n**Investigation summary:** The rca-context.json in this eval case described a different error group (pymilvus, group 03) rather than the actual transformers group (group 02). I used the actual job data from `groups/02-fromager-bootstrap-fails-to-resolve-transformers-5-6-0/` directly. The root cause is a stale `transformers<5` constraint that was not updated when vllm was bumped from 0.21.0 to 0.24.0, the latter of which now requires `transformers>=5.6.0`. Both affected jobs (aarch64 and x86_64) fail identically